# Jak II: the menu pointer on the title's menu (LIST-0.1.1 item 19; the owner: "i want the pointer to be able to
# interact with all menus"). Start, then A once the title is ready (as jak2_melee.sim), opens its menu; the right hand
# turns from high to low (the dot down the panel 1.6 m ahead), a shot at each height: the row under the dot is the one
# picked (highlighted). Then the dot back on the lowest row (Quit Game; at -20 it is under the menu, where the trigger
# picks nothing) and the trigger: its Yes / No line comes up under it. Then at 4, 2 and 0 degrees (the line is a little
# under the row's name: JAKVR_POINTER_TRACE=1 logs the dot against the line's middle) the dot to the left half (12
# degrees: Yes) and the right half (-4: No; -12 is past the line's end), a shot each, and last the trigger on No, which
# closes the question (a click on Yes would quit the game).
2400 menu 1
2406 menu 0
2900 a 1
2906 a 0
3100 shot jm-main
3120 hand_pitch 30
3150 shot jm-p30
3160 hand_pitch 20
3190 shot jm-p20
3200 hand_pitch 10
3230 shot jm-p10
3240 hand_pitch 0
3270 shot jm-p0
3280 hand_pitch -10
3310 shot jm-pm10
3320 hand_pitch -20
3350 shot jm-pm20
3360 hand_pitch 0
3380 right_trigger 1
3386 right_trigger 0
3440 shot jm-exit-asked
3445 hand_pitch 4
3450 hand_yaw 12
3480 shot jm-exit-4-yes
3490 hand_yaw -4
3520 shot jm-exit-4-no
3525 hand_pitch 2
3530 hand_yaw 12
3560 shot jm-exit-2-yes
3570 hand_yaw -4
3600 shot jm-exit-2-no
3605 hand_pitch 0
3610 hand_yaw 12
3640 shot jm-exit-0-yes
3650 hand_yaw -4
3680 shot jm-exit-0-no
3685 hand_pitch 2
3700 right_trigger 1
3706 right_trigger 0
3760 shot jm-exit-closed
3800 quit 0
